1
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:19,560
Honda, don't let Honda and those
old geezers get ahead of you.

2
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:20,000
Yes.

3
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:23,280
Kawa?

4
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:25,380
Kawa, Senior Suyo.

5
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:27,480
Yeah, we crossed the river, though.

6
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:28,580
Senior, what's that?

7
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:30,720
Those guys.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,500
Hey there, Honda and the old geezers.

9
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:36,460
Well done. You've already escaped?

10
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:39,240
I'm going to give you a
proper thank-you for earlier.

11
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:40,200
Let's go.

12
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:44,160
Showa Battle, go!

13
00:01:09,540 --> 00:01:11,480
Are you all right, senpai?

14
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:13,280
That goddamn old man!

15
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:16,400
Just give up and go home, go home!

16
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:20,340
Kankichi Ryotsu isn't the
type to give up that easily.

17
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:22,200
We've got a trump card.

18
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:25,040
A trump card? Where is it?

19
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:26,080
It's you.

20
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:27,400
Hey, Bobobobobo.

21
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,100
Me?

22
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:30,200
No, no, no.

23
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:32,960
No, no, no.

24
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:34,000
No.

25
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:36,720
It flew! Grab the stick!

26
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:38,160
There are plenty of those.

27
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:38,580
No.

28
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:41,140
This feeling...

29
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:44,580
Alright!

30
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:46,180
Here we go!

31
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:49,680
Hey, hold on tight!

32
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:51,240
Let's go!

33
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:53,420
Dosuwea!

34
00:01:57,360 --> 00:02:00,420
My body can handle it,
so speed it up even more!

35
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:03,520
S-Shia!

36
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,980
They're coming at an incredible speed!

37
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,880
Spread out! Firing line!

38
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:11,040
Funny hunting!

39
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:13,040
What, a special attack!?

40
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:22,240
Did you see that?
The bookshelf sword secret art!

41
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:26,680
Those bastards!

42
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:29,820
What secret art? You just threw a rock!

43
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:32,600
Senpai, this is no time for that!

44
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:33,840
What?

45
00:02:36,260 --> 00:02:38,320
This time it's really over, Kankichi Ryotsu!

46
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:40,020
Well then, farewell!

47
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:41,540
Here it comes!

48
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:44,540
Ugh!

49
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:46,620
Eeek!

50
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:48,600
Senpai!

51
00:02:49,020 --> 00:02:51,460
Damn it! Isn't there some good move?!

52
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:52,840
No, wait, I've got it.

53
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:54,200
What? What is it?

54
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:57,280
Here goes!

55
00:02:57,300 --> 00:02:58,000
Pabu!

56
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:03,540
Nobody knows

57
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:08,460
From the southern sea

58
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:09,920
Senpai! This song!

59
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:12,160
There's no doubt! He's here!

60
00:03:42,320 --> 00:03:44,120
This factory is as long as ever, isn't it.

61
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:45,800
Hahahaha!

62
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:47,380
Ryotsu!

63
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:49,520
Don't worry, I'm here now.

64
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:50,600
Peep-peep!

65
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:54,160
Ugh!

66
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:01,300
A biker showing off his stunts.

67
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:06,020
Ugh, lately if I don't do this, my dolphin
underlings won't listen to a word I say.

68
00:04:06,660 --> 00:04:08,780
Enough already, hurry up and save me!

69
00:04:16,620 --> 00:04:40,360
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu...

70
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:45,240
Well then, have a nice day!

71
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:52,620
Anyway, we're saved.
Honda, we're going after Honda's old man!

72
00:04:52,940 --> 00:04:54,820
Ugh, can't we just go home already?

73
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:58,740
Idiot! We've come this far, how can we quit?
Let's go!

74
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,360
Yeah, yeah, I get it.

75
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:06,960
Nooo!

76
00:05:07,860 --> 00:05:10,380
W-what is that sound?

77
00:05:10,380 --> 00:05:12,380
It might be the footsteps of a dinosaur.

78
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:13,120
Right?

79
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,160
No doubt about it.

80
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:18,560
This way!

81
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,240
Let's go!

82
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:20,000
No way...

83
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:27,720
Senpai

84
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:28,840
Desert

85
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:31,440
What's going on with this island?

86
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:36,240
But the dinosaur tracks really do lead off past the dunes,
don't they?

87
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:39,200
What are those tire-like
tracks in the middle?

88
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:42,320
It's that old man Hontarō
from the north, I bet.

89
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:46,300
Didn't he prepare a three-wheeler
for the desert or something?

90
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:50,120
If that's the case,
we'll fall even further behind!

91
00:05:50,160 --> 00:05:51,260
Let's go, Honda!

92
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:54,820
What are you doing? Hurry up and come!

93
00:05:54,940 --> 00:05:56,160
Coming, coming!

94
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:02,680
Ugh, this heat is unbearable.

95
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:08,300
Damn it, my body...

96
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:14,540
Honda, give me some water.

97
00:06:14,540 --> 00:06:17,060
Senpai, over here too!

98
00:06:17,060 --> 00:06:18,680
What a disaster.

99
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:21,920
Senpai, let's just go back to Japan already.

100
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:24,000
There's no way we can
go back empty-handed now!

101
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:27,020
If we cross these dunes,
there might be water.

102
00:06:27,020 --> 00:06:28,020
Let's go.

103
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:36,500
Honda and the others are
the old man's disciples!

104
00:06:39,460 --> 00:06:40,540
It's the Honda-ra old geezers!

105
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:43,540
So he was on foot too?

106
00:06:43,540 --> 00:06:45,960
Alright, Honda! Let's catch up at once!

107
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:50,120
Hey, Honda, what's wrong?

108
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:51,560
I can't take another step.

109
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:54,620
Pull yourself together, we're almost there!

110
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:57,600
Here you go.

111
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,680
The Honda-ra old geezers!

112
00:07:04,380 --> 00:07:06,220
Ryotsu, you're alive?

113
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:08,920
Ryotsu Kankichi-sama isn't
going down that easily!

114
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:11,300
I'll catch the boss myself!

115
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:13,380
No way I'm losing!

116
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:14,940
You lecherous kappa!

117
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:16,440
You perverted gorilla!

118
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:17,700
It's this wisdom that counts!

119
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:19,480
Countermeasure, you pervert!

120
00:07:28,280 --> 00:07:29,860
I've got no strength left.

121
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:31,320
Is this where it ends?

122
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:36,740
What?

123
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:44,320
Welcome!

124
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:46,400
Not you again.

125
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:49,800
You look pretty beat.

126
00:07:49,800 --> 00:07:51,540
At our oasis of... whatever this is,

127
00:07:51,540 --> 00:07:55,360
we've got mineral water, cola,
juice, oolong tea, and more!

128
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:56,700
Come on, have a drink.

129
00:07:56,700 --> 00:07:57,960
Hmm-hmm.

130
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:01,060
Drink up, drink up, yeah!

131
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:01,240
What?

132
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:06,980
What are you doing?

133
00:08:08,580 --> 00:08:10,580
This won't come free, you know.

134
00:08:10,820 --> 00:08:12,660
It's ten thousand yen a cup.

135
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:14,740
Ten thousand yen?

136
00:08:15,020 --> 00:08:17,260
Are you trying to take advantage
of people's weaknesses again?

137
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:21,940
Take it, you thief!

138
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:23,280
Don't pay for it!

139
00:08:25,980 --> 00:08:26,800
Thank you for your business.

140
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:29,260
Here you go.

141
00:08:33,020 --> 00:08:34,540
I'm revived!

142
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:39,420
Look at this nimble footwork! Farewell!

143
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:46,360
I'll drink it by force if I have to!

144
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:56,300
I've got no business with people who have no money!
Farewell!

145
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:58,880
Damn it, that's dirty!

146
00:08:59,360 --> 00:09:00,060
Hey, Honda!

147
00:09:04,060 --> 00:09:06,800
Oh right, I still have this conch shell.

148
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:09,880
Someone come help!

149
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:27,540
It's hopeless, I don't even have
the strength to blow the conch shell.

150
00:09:31,380 --> 00:09:32,100
That's...

151
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:40,380
It's not a bulge in my crotch.

152
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:42,340
An incident has occurred on land!

153
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:44,820
Everything's solved with just a swim trunk!

154
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:47,720
Swim-Trunk Detective Harai has arrived!

155
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:52,900
Glad you came, Swim-Trunk Detective.

156
00:09:52,900 --> 00:09:54,640
What's up? What do you want, Ryotsu?

157
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:57,060
As you can see, my throat's bone dry.

158
00:09:57,540 --> 00:10:01,400
My stomach's empty, and Honda and I are about to die.
Please help us.

159
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:04,280
Yes, the conch shell I blew
came in handy after all.

160
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:05,020
Good.

161
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:07,040
Here.

162
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:10,220
Gah! How can you pull ramen out from there?

163
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:13,200
Don't worry about the details. Now eat up.

164
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:15,540
It's special seafood ramen,
straight from my swim trunks.

165
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:18,740
I wish you'd made it chilled
Chinese noodles instead.

166
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:25,200
Spicy!

167
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:27,160
Spicy, spicy, spicy!

168
00:10:28,960 --> 00:10:30,880
Didn't it suit your taste?

169
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:33,560
I've been researching
extra-spicy ramen lately.

170
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:35,440
Don't feed us extra-spicy
food at a time like this!

171
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:37,040
Give me water, water!

172
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:38,680
You're a demanding one, aren't you?

173
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:39,460
Well then,

174
00:10:39,460 --> 00:10:41,680
Come on, drink up!

175
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:46,420
I'm not surprised by anything that comes
out of a swimsuit pocket at this point,

176
00:10:46,780 --> 00:10:49,020
but being told to drink from that spot...

177
00:10:49,020 --> 00:10:51,680
I told you not to sweat the small stuff!

178
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:52,620
But...

179
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:57,700
Here, drink up.

180
00:10:59,940 --> 00:11:01,060
I'll take some.

181
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:05,260
Got a cold.

182
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:11,260
Anyway, we're saved.

183
00:11:11,860 --> 00:11:13,660
Thanks, Kaipandegaa.

184
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:14,340
Thank you very much.

185
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:14,900
Thank you very much.

186
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:17,200
If you're ever in trouble, just call us.

187
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,940
Well then, farewell.

188
00:11:22,580 --> 00:11:25,120
Senpai, we really were saved.

189
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:27,320
He's a pervert, but a good guy.

190
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:30,720
Right, once we're back on our feet,
let's go find the boss.

191
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:31,440
Yes!

192
00:11:40,140 --> 00:11:42,440
The footprints end here, don't they?

193
00:11:44,340 --> 00:11:45,440
Whoever climbed the cliff face

194
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:48,740
Old man Hontarō!

195
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:50,360
P-please, go ahead!

196
00:11:50,740 --> 00:11:52,300
Ugh, what a persistent bastard.

197
00:11:52,760 --> 00:11:53,660
Hey there, you dirty old geezer!

198
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:55,840
We're catching up now,
so you'd better be ready, damn it!

199
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:56,680
Like hell we'll let you!

200
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:01,520
It's Nessie!

201
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:02,720
Honda, the rope!

202
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:03,160
Yes!

203
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:07,520
I'll catch Nessie myself!

204
00:12:07,780 --> 00:12:08,800
Hold on, I'm coming!

205
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:09,440
Yah!

206
00:12:11,760 --> 00:12:12,440
Alright, we've got it!

207
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:13,840
Let's go, Honda!

208
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:26,440
This guy's so persistent in this race!

209
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:29,860
What do you think you're doing?

210
00:12:30,300 --> 00:12:31,920
Just fall already!

211
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:32,620
Stop it!

212
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:43,460
Phew, that saved us!

213
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:45,500
How about it?

214
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:47,220
An egg!

215
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:50,880
Alright!
Then I won't forgive that old geezer!

216
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:52,180
Yah!

217
00:12:53,700 --> 00:12:55,180
There, there...

218
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:55,760
Gah!

219
00:12:55,980 --> 00:12:57,160
Not this time, Ryo-san!

220
00:12:57,780 --> 00:12:58,660
Chaaaaaa!

221
00:12:58,660 --> 00:12:58,800
Woooooh!

222
00:12:59,620 --> 00:13:01,940
Nyahahaha! Well, just watch!

223
00:13:02,060 --> 00:13:03,980
This next one's the finishing blow! Heh heh!

224
00:13:04,760 --> 00:13:05,600
Here I go!

225
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:07,000
Senpai...

226
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:08,900
Behind you...

227
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:09,800
Ah...

228
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:10,180
What is it?

229
00:13:10,820 --> 00:13:11,220
Whoaaaaa!

230
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:14,760
I'll return this to you.

231
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:16,940
Thanks.

232
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:21,920
Stop it!

233
00:13:21,920 --> 00:13:23,600
Ow ow!

234
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:23,940
Quit it!

235
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:24,960
Quit it!

236
00:13:28,860 --> 00:13:50,800

No no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no no

237
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:58,960
Oh no

238
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:05,720
Doing it to yourself like that,
what an idiot.

239
00:14:09,820 --> 00:14:12,320
Heave-ho, shut!

240
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:13,040
Thank you very much.

241
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:16,440
Now, where did that Nessie go?

242
00:14:17,620 --> 00:14:18,700
Senpai!

243
00:14:18,700 --> 00:14:19,360
It's Nessie.

244
00:14:22,020 --> 00:14:23,060
No doubt about it!

245
00:14:23,820 --> 00:14:25,560
We've finally cornered Nessie!

246
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:26,180
Let's go!

247
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:26,660
Yes!

248
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:28,720
What's this music?

249
00:14:35,840 --> 00:14:38,520
Hahaha! Long time no see, Ryotsu!

250
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:40,860
I knew it was you, Colonel Paguryu!

251
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:43,800
Why are you even here?!

252
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:47,480
At the request of the US government,
I came to capture a dinosaur alive.

253
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:49,820
What?! No way!

254
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:54,660
We've come this far, and no matter what happened,
my lord and I

255
00:14:55,580 --> 00:14:59,000
Fine, then. I'll just take it by force.

256
00:15:04,780 --> 00:15:06,880
Then you'll have to give up too.

257
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:20,420
Honda, yes, I really don't want to call him,
but we're bringing in the sky specialist too.

258
00:15:32,540 --> 00:15:34,640
Bathing in the moon's energy on my back,

259
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:36,860
justice's steps tear through the darkness!

260
00:15:36,860 --> 00:15:39,300
Leave the skies to us!

261
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:41,880
Moonlight Deka, reporting for duty!

262
00:15:41,880 --> 00:15:44,980
Venus Deka, his assistant, is here too!

263
00:15:45,340 --> 00:15:47,280
What are those guys? They're in the way!

264
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:48,000
Take this!

265
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:54,940
Useless bunch!

266
00:15:58,480 --> 00:15:59,980
Alright, break 'em!

267
00:16:06,860 --> 00:16:08,780
Our Moonlight!

268
00:16:09,220 --> 00:16:12,360
Can't be helped!
Let's transform, Venus Deka!

269
00:16:12,540 --> 00:16:13,060
Right!

270
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:16,580
Moonlight Power!

271
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:18,520
Make up!

272
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:27,620
Master Tetsumen

273
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:31,000
By transforming into a female Nezumi Kozo,
Moonlight Deka

274
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:33,260
gets much faster at making his escape.

275
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:37,620
He's gone!

276
00:16:37,620 --> 00:16:40,980
But even if a man dresses
up as a female Nezumi Kozo,

277
00:16:40,980 --> 00:16:43,300
isn't he just a regular Nezumi Kozo?

278
00:16:44,300 --> 00:17:01,700
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

279
00:17:02,160 --> 00:17:03,960
The forest is so dense, but I can see them.

280
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:07,900
Heave!

281
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:08,980
Heave-ho!

282
00:17:10,140 --> 00:17:10,780
Senpai

283
00:17:10,780 --> 00:17:12,760
What exactly are you going to do?

284
00:17:13,340 --> 00:17:14,580
Did it to Colonel Paguryu.

285
00:17:14,580 --> 00:17:15,640
Let's get it revving!

286
00:17:16,320 --> 00:17:16,640
Alright!

287
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:17,760
Honda

288
00:17:18,980 --> 00:17:20,700
Pull that rope with all your might!

289
00:17:25,260 --> 00:17:25,580
Alright.

290
00:17:25,580 --> 00:17:26,120
Stop!

291
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:27,260
Listen, Honda!

292
00:17:27,260 --> 00:17:29,120
When the colonel's Apache comes back,

293
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:30,520
let go of that rope.

294
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:33,540
Now!

295
00:17:37,860 --> 00:17:39,580
Magryu-Daizer!

296
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:41,460
Prepare yourselves!

297
00:17:42,340 --> 00:17:42,860
What?

298
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:46,380
No way!

299
00:17:48,940 --> 00:17:52,940
I've gone and cut another
worthless thing. Stop.

300
00:17:57,120 --> 00:17:58,660
The seat's going to hit!

301
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:02,280
Aaaaah!

302
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:10,580
Senpai, this is a disaster! The
colonel's helicopter collided and exploded!

303
00:18:10,580 --> 00:18:12,060
Aaaaah!

304
00:18:18,860 --> 00:18:20,040
He's still alive?

305
00:18:20,040 --> 00:18:46,040


306
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:47,140
Princess Lovey-Dovey!

307
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:56,440
Nessie was fake?

308
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:57,960
Hey, you!

309
00:18:58,760 --> 00:19:00,580
What's the meaning of this?

310
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:02,120
S-sorry!

311
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:04,740
There are various circumstances behind this!

312
00:19:05,420 --> 00:19:06,940
Well, explain it clearly!

313
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:08,140
Not that!

314
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:10,960
Gah!

315
00:19:12,820 --> 00:19:13,560
Ew

316
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:17,244
What's the problem? This isn't
"Princess Onoroki,"

317
00:19:17,294 --> 00:19:19,100
it's "Granny Odoroki"!

318
00:19:19,280 --> 00:19:21,240
Hey, what's going on here?

319
00:19:21,540 --> 00:19:21,994
Well,

320
00:19:22,044 --> 00:19:26,080
lately the tourists visiting
the island have dwindled badly.

321
00:19:26,480 --> 00:19:30,420
So we figured we'd stir up a dinosaur
commotion to draw crowds and make some money.

322
00:19:31,780 --> 00:19:32,500
That's all there is to it.

323
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:35,920
Everyone, we're running away!

324
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:41,560
Damn it, they're so fast at running away!

325
00:19:45,220 --> 00:19:47,440
Colonel, take us with you too!

326
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:50,980
You crashed my Apache and
you have the nerve to say that?

327
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:54,360
Farewell!

328
00:19:54,360 --> 00:19:55,100
Hey, you...

329
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:55,700
Wait!

330
00:19:58,340 --> 00:19:59,800
He's really gone

331
00:20:00,860 --> 00:20:03,800
Senpai, what's going to happen to us?

332
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:08,160
No choice,
let's have Nakagawa come pick us up.

333
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:09,820
Naetsuka, what about the west?

334
00:20:18,420 --> 00:20:20,680
It's better not to come back here right now.

335
00:20:21,320 --> 00:20:23,740
Why don't you stay over
there until things cool down?

336
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:27,820
Well, there's no choice.
We'll live on this island for a while.

337
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:30,560
Damn you, this thing!

338
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:34,660
Goddamn it!

339
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:42,240
Senpai, that voice just now!

340
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:44,780
It was just a hollow prop with a tape stuffed inside,
wasn't it?

341
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:46,140
Alright, let's go!

342
00:20:48,620 --> 00:20:51,460
Well, that was a total waste of effort.

343
00:20:51,840 --> 00:20:53,561
After all, a real dinosaur...

344
00:20:53,611 --> 00:20:56,200
couldn't possibly still be alive in this world,
could it?

